# Secrets for Qubit Agent (Qubit VoiceBridge). NEVER commit real values.
#
# All voice processing (ASR, VAD, voice-ID, TTS, short replies) is fully LOCAL.
# These two keys are only needed for the OPTIONAL cloud paths:
#   - DeepSeek API   -> long/complex conversation answers (fast, ~1s)
#   - Perplexity API -> current-info/web questions ("what's the latest news...")
# Without them the bridge still works: short turns are answered by the local
# qubit-brain4 model; agent task routing is unaffected.

# The bridge reads these from ~/.config/qubit-voicebridge/.env by default (see
# config: intent.deepseek_env / intent.perplexity_env). A legacy ~/.hermes/.env
# is still honored when the canonical file is absent, with a loud migration
# warning. Create the canonical file:
#
#   echo 'DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...'    >> ~/.config/qubit-voicebridge/.env
#   echo 'PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=pplx-...' >> ~/.config/qubit-voicebridge/.env
#
# Get keys at:
#   DeepSeek:    https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
#   Perplexity:  https://www.perplexity.ai/settings/api

DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# Optional: OpenAI key — only used if you enable the (removed/legacy)
# Realtime lane or edge-tts alternatives. Not required for the local stack.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
